165
00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:47.460
So you'll do, what, usually, like, four to seven takes per camera setup?

166
00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:48.020
Mm-hmm.

167
00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.380
Because, you know, and then you move the cameras and you do it again.

168
00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:52.840
But that blew my mind.

169
00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:59.360
He said that we started at 7 a.m., wrapped around 7.30, and managed to shoot seven and

170
00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:03.560
four-eighths pages, which I guess is a fancy way to say seven and a half.

171
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:04.040
Okay.

172
00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:08.620
Fast fact number two, Rainn Wilson was very sick for this episode.

173
00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.480
Very, very sick.

174
00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.500
So we just explained to you everything that went into planning this workday.

175
00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.480
Guess what happened?

176
00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:16.860
Yeah.

177
00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:17.460
Oh, yeah.

178
00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:17.820
Go.

179
00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.520
We had to—they had it all scheduled, and then they had to cancel it.

180
00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.640
And reschedule it for a different day by a week.

181
00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.620
Not just cancel it, like, a few days ahead.

182
00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:34.900
Basically, Rainn was sick the beginning of the episode, and then the day this was scheduled,

183
00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.760
if I remember, it was sort of like on a Wednesday or Thursday.

184
00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:43.380
We'd already done some office scenes in the bullpen, and we were going later—

185
00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.540
I think it was a Wednesday.

186
00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:44.940
Yeah.

187
00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:50.120
I reached out to Kent about this as well, and he said he always liked to put these

188
00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.000
location shoots on a Tuesday or a Wednesday.

189
00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:53.680
Yes.

190
00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.120
And go ahead.

191
00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.400
That's what I remember, too.

192
00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.280
It was like a Wednesday.

193
00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.720
But we'd already been filming in the bullpen Monday, Tuesday, like the main office building.

194
00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.760
And I remember we only had the hotel for one day.

195
00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.360
It was a big deal because they had to reserve this room and everything.

196
00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:09.920
Yes.

197
00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.920
And then we had all the extras hired and everything.

198
00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:21.320
I woke up Wednesday morning, and I got a call from our second AD, and they said,

199
00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:23.220
Angela, the hotel's been canceled.

200
00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.320
Rainn is too sick.

201
00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:25.720
He's too sick.

202
00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.220
Like, his doctor said, you cannot go.

203
00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.560
And I was like, oh, my gosh.

204
00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.120
And so they were sort of scrambling now to figure out what Wednesday was going to look like.

205
00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:38.840
Well, I got a call at home, Jenna, the hotel has been canceled.

206
00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.300
You need to come in to work.

207
00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.320
We're going to be shooting back in the office now.

208
00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:42.540
Yeah.

209
00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.120
So I got the day off.

210
00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:45.660
And I suddenly had to work.

211
00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:47.280
Yes.

212
00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:52.840
Well, I actually called Rainn about it, and he said that it is the only time in 10 years

213
00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:57.100
of working on the office that he was not able to come to work for a day.

214
00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.020
But he had a fever over 102.

215
00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:03.040
He said a doctor came and said, you cannot go to work.

216
00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.920
Rainn has a fantastic work ethic, and I don't doubt that.

217
00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.500
For him to miss, he was very ill.

218
00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:12.380
Well, we had a fan question from Chris Bodnar, who kind of clocked it.

219
00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.020
He said, was Rainn Wilson sick during this episode because his voice sounds like he might

220
00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:16.720
have a cold?

221
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:23.860
And Rainn said, actually, the voice thing is because he was screaming during the speech,

222
00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.900
and he kind of blew out his voice.

223
00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.480
But you can actually hear in the conference room before we ever move to the hotel.

224
00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.460
You can tell he's coming down with it.

225
00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.160
I could really tell.

226
00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.720
I heard his voice in the conference room.

227
00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.780
That's before we went to the hotel, and he sounded legit sick.

228
00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:38.960
So I agree with you, Chris.

229
00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:44.100
I wonder if he got a phone call from Greg Daniels telling him it was his finest performance

230
00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.340
because he's really good in this episode.

231
00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.220
He's really, really good in this episode.

232
00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:53.100
But yeah, I mean, the other thing, too, you should know is that Rainn really didn't want

233
00:09:53.100 --> 00:10:00.000
to miss work because he knew how much went into that day, the extras, the hotel, the location

234
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.420
shoot.

235
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.700
So I think he was-

236
00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:02.220
The dummy wranglers.

237
00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:03.060
The dummy wranglers.

238
00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.680
I think he was really trying to power it out, and then his body just couldn't.

239
00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:07.080
Yeah.

240
00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:08.520
All right.

241
00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.240
Fast fact number three.

