Creed.

1567
01:02:52.510 --> 01:02:53.990
Why did I miss that?

1568
01:02:54.190 --> 01:02:57.830
Creed goes over there and adjusts the thermostat.

1569
01:02:58.030 --> 01:02:59.730
He's the last one.

1570
01:02:59.750 --> 01:03:01.310
I missed that.

1571
01:03:02.230 --> 01:03:12.470
Well, at the very end of this episode, Jim is passing by Pam's desk, and Pam says, oh, I've always wanted to go to Australia.

1572
01:03:13.010 --> 01:03:14.450
And he says, well, I'm going.

1573
01:03:14.450 --> 01:03:16.230
I bought a non-refundable ticket.

1574
01:03:16.590 --> 01:03:21.810
And this is when he tells us he bought his ticket for June 8th.

1575
01:03:22.010 --> 01:03:23.990
Oh, the look on Pam's face.

1576
01:03:23.990 --> 01:03:25.670
Her wedding is June 10th.

1577
01:03:25.670 --> 01:03:27.690
I mean, this is so telling.

1578
01:03:27.910 --> 01:03:35.930
I mean, Pam, if Pam had any doubts at all that this was hard on him, she can't deny it anymore.

1579
01:03:36.070 --> 01:03:37.030
Yeah, he's leaving.

1580
01:03:37.270 --> 01:03:43.270
He has basically said to her, I'm sorry, but I cannot be there when you marry someone else.

1581
01:03:43.390 --> 01:03:44.270
I can't be there.

1582
01:03:44.470 --> 01:03:51.610
In fact, I have to be on basically the farthest spot on the earth from your wedding.

1583
01:03:51.730 --> 01:03:51.890
Yeah.

1584
01:03:51.890 --> 01:03:56.670
I'm going to go halfway around the world to get away from your wedding.

1585
01:03:56.890 --> 01:03:59.670
I mean, it just gutted me.

1586
01:03:59.810 --> 01:04:04.750
And I just wanted to shake Pam and be like, if you don't know now, then you'll never know.

1587
01:04:04.770 --> 01:04:05.790
He loves you.

1588
01:04:06.070 --> 01:04:07.690
But I think it's more than that.

1589
01:04:07.830 --> 01:04:16.250
I think what's happening is Jim is saying, I'm not sure how to even be your friend now that you're getting married.

1590
01:04:16.250 --> 01:04:22.710
Like, I know we're best friends at the office, but I'm not going to come to your wedding.

1591
01:04:22.710 --> 01:04:26.810
And when you're married, I'm not going to hang with you.

1592
01:04:27.310 --> 01:04:28.550
He's, you know.

1593
01:04:28.750 --> 01:04:32.390
I think what he's finally admitting is they're not best friends.

1594
01:04:32.610 --> 01:04:33.430
Yeah, they can't.

1595
01:04:33.430 --> 01:04:34.630
How can they be?

1596
01:04:34.870 --> 01:04:36.470
They've crossed this line.

1597
01:04:36.730 --> 01:04:38.430
They've had that moment on Booze Cruise.

1598
01:04:38.870 --> 01:04:42.530
They've had these moments now, and the line has been crossed.

1599
